      "Language": "ita",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "In double-blind conditions, ST-679 (a single oral 1200 mg dose in 20 patients), or paracetamol (a single oral dose of 1000 mg in 20 patients) was administered to forty patients who presented pain as a result of obstetrical-gynecological surgery. The study proposed to evaluate the analgesic efficacy and tolerability of ST-679, a new non-steroid antiphlogistic drug, as compared to a reference drug amply utilized in clinical practice such as paracetamol. The average estimation of tolerability, with regard to paracetamol, was significantly in favor of ST-679."},
